requiredFindings.counterexample:
Replace the EE-1 site with:
let explicitly_trusted = claim.provenance.source_class == SourceClass::ExplicitlyTrusted;
compare(work)?;
if tested(explicitly_trusted)
    && !probe(policy.explicitly_trusted, claim.provenance.publisher, work)?
{ /* unchanged refusal */ }
The stored boolean is computed before the potentially refused charge. Successful output, ledger sequence and operation-log sequence stay identical. With a short allowance, the extra computation is invisible because tested is not reached. The same pattern applies to the EE-5a boolean tests.
